#: theory.md:1
msgid "Volume-based Metadynamics intro and theory"
msgstr "Volume-based Metadynamics の導入と理論"

#: theory.md:3
msgid ""
"In Metadynamics, one of the most important decisions the user must make is "
"selecting an appropriate collective variable (CV) that can comprehensively "
"describe the slow degrees of freedom relevant to the phenomenon of interest."
" When focusing on protein-ligand (or more generally, host-guest) binding, "
"significant effort has been dedicated to identifying CVs, often based on "
"human intuition and/or data-driven techniques."
msgstr ""
"Metadynamics では、対象現象の遅い自由度を十分に記述する適切な Collective Variable (CV) "
"の選択が重要です。Protein-Ligand、一般には Host-Guest の結合では、直感やデータに基づく技術により CV "
"の特定に多くの努力が払われてきました。"

#: theory.md:5
msgid ""
"In VMetaD, the choice is simplified: the CVs are the 3D coordinates of the "
"ligand's center of mass relative to a reference frame defined by the host. "
"The primary goal of VMetaD is to identify all possible binding and unbinding"
" pathways quickly and reliably, and this approach is tailored to that "
"objective."
msgstr ""
"VMetaD は選択を単純化し、Host が定める参照座標系での Ligand の Center of Mass の3次元座標を CV "
"とします。すべての結合・解離経路を速く確実に見つけるという目的に適した方法です。"

#: theory.md:7
msgid ""
"The main problem in this approach is given by the time needed for VMetaD to "
"\"fill\" the unbound state, allowing recrossing events: if the host is "
"immersed in a reasonably large box, the (long) time needed to observe a "
"favorable binding event makes this technique completely useless. For this "
"reason, a restraining potential is applied (usually at the center of mass of"
" the host), which limits the conformational space and allows the guest to "
"enter and exit the host in an efficient manner. The shape of such "
"restraining potential strongly depends in what is the problem or how much "
"information the user knows about the system. In the [original "
"implementation](https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jpclett.9b01183) (and in this "
"tutorial) we implemented a spherical-shaped restraint and used spherical "
"coordinates as CVs. In a [subsequent "
"work](https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.1c00649) we used a parabolic "
"potential and parabolic coordinates as CVs. In the case of the sphere, we "
"have the restraining potential defined as"
msgstr ""
"問題は、非結合状態を埋めて Recrossing を可能にする時間です。大きな Box "
"では、好都合な結合を観測するまでが長すぎて実用になりません。そのため通常 Host の Center of Mass を中心に Restraint "
"Potential を置き、空間を制限して Guest "
"が効率よく出入りできるようにします。形は問題や既知情報に依存します。[原著](https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jpclett.9b01183)"
" とこの Tutorial では球形 Restraint と球座標 CV "
"を使い、[後続研究](https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.1c00649) では放物線 Potential "
"と放物線座標を使いました。球では、Restraint Potential は次のとおりです。"

#: theory.md:18
msgid ""
"where $k$ is the harmonic constant, $\\rho(t)$ is the distance of the guest "
"center of mass from the center of the restraining sphere, and "
"$\\rho_{\\text{s}}$ is the radius of the restraining sphere."
msgstr ""
"$k$ は Harmonic Constant、$\\rho(t)$ は Guest の Center of Mass "
"と球の中心との距離、$\\rho_{\\text{s}}$ は球の半径です。"

#: theory.md:20
msgid ""
"Given enough simulation time, this setup alone can return all the possible "
"binding and unbinding pathways (if that is the only goal). However, "
"considering the fact that VMetaD builds a history-dependent potential, we "
"can also compute the free energy difference between the bound and unbound "
"states (i.e. the binding free energy) when we are at convergence. The main "
"point here is to identify the unbound state in a comprehensive way (we "
"assume that the bound state is well defined in volume). To do this, we "
"reweight the converged free energy landscape and project it onto some new "
"CVs that allow better identification and discrimination of both the bound "
"and unbound states."
msgstr ""
"十分な時間があれば、この設定だけですべての結合・解離経路を得られます。さらに VMetaD は履歴依存 Potential "
"を作るため、収束すれば結合・非結合状態の自由エネルギー差、すなわち結合自由エネルギーも求められます。結合状態の体積は明確と仮定し、非結合状態を十分に特定することが重要です。収束した地形を"
" Reweighting し、両状態をよりよく識別する新しい CV に射影します。"

